WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm definitely gonna be the first-star idol!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.520
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.400
So far on Aikatsu Stars!

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.780
Just the other day, Yuzu-senpai held an event for her brand, Shiny Smile.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:24.170
There I got to see Hime-senpai, Yozora-senpai, and Tsubasa-senpai all together for the first time in a while.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:28.540
Not only that, but Yuzu-senpai got Star Wings too.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.170
The Saturn Star Premium Rare Coord was captivating.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.090
Our senpai really are amazing.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.760
But we can't let them stay ahead forever.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.600
We'll heat up our Aikatsu even more throughout the summer!

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.810
Proficiency tests?

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:49.440
Yeah, they're held regularly at Venus Ark.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.860
They're next week!

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:59.620
We need to find time to study between work and lessons. It won't be easy.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:04.000
I mean, Four Star Academy had the occasional test too...

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.170
I wonder what these are like.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.210
The idols here come from a lot of different countries, right?

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:13.460
Test subjects are chosen based on where they're from.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.180
Different countries have different test subjects?

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:22.140
Yeah! For example, Kirara-chan is from 
New Zealand, so she's fluent in English.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:27.190
She'll be given English as her language arts, and then German as her foreign language.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.980
So what about us...

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.400
Language arts, math, and English.{not Japanese?}{because, as I'm sure you noticed immediately after, different countries}

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.700
That's pretty normal. What a relief.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.780
Congratulation.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.870
You act as though you've already passed.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.490
Juli-senpai!

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:48.210
Students at Venus Ark must constantly be top-level in everything under the sun.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:49.630
Sh-She's fast!

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.090
And her posture is rock solid! {oops}

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:59.640
Owing to Elza-sama's unending pursuit of perfection, Venus Ark's proficiency tests are not to be underestimated.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:03.350
You would do best to prepare accordingly.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:47.450
Look, everyone is studying.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.500
You're right.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.000
Kirara-chan.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.750
Oh, Yume-chan.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.420
Hello, Caroline.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.670
Even you're studying, Kirara?

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.050
Yeah, the tests are coming up.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.760
Are the tests really that hard?

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.850
You need 800 points combined to pass.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:11.930
But a lot of students only barely make it even after lots of cramming.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:17.190
And that's not even the scariest part...

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:26.450
If you don't pass, you'll be locked in the unimaginably horrifying forbidden room until your grades improve!

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.530
Th-That gets... me going.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.080
What forbidden room?

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.450
It's in the hold!

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:35.460
Nobody's used it in forever, so they call it the forbidden room.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.750
Anyway, if you get close to it...

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.250
Baa!

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.300
Something might be inside!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.380
It's definitely, definitely baa!

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.510
What do you mean, "something"?!

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:48.930
Is that true?

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.140
I think it's just a rumor.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:54.350
Still, knowing Elza-san...

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.020
It could be real!

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.780
Today's steak is made from Saga beef.{I feel like there's a better to this but I don't an expert}{I didn't actually check the CCs, but Saga does exist, so... oh you meant the formation}

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:04.110
Thank you.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:08.660
How do you think the Four Star girls will do on the proficiency tests?

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.660
I wonder if they'll be okay.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:16.330
If they don't do good enough, they'll get a special baa!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.290
Right, Elza-sama?

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:21.920
Yes, I will not show any mercy.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:25.800
Here.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.220
Problem sets for what's on the test.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.350
What?! All of these?

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:35.430
I have to take a design test in addition to this, so I'll be off reviewing for it.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:37.810
You've got it rough, Koharu.

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.730
Let's all do our best!

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:40.730
Yeah!

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.690
Now then...

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:51.030
This is really gonna be tough. 
Only a week until the tests.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:55.040
We still have work and lessons too, so we'll need to study efficiently.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.710
How can we do that?

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:01.750
Like for instance, we could get really good tutors...

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.340
That's it, Rola!

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:08.800
There are plenty of special people all around us!

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.970
First up is language arts.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.890
Why are we at a park?

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:17.560
Our teacher told us to meet here.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.100
Teacher?

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.900
A German poet once said:

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:26.280
"The best way to learn is to teach." {First of all, this formation is from Oppenheimer, an American scientist. Second, this is actually a quote from Seneca of ancient Rome}{he uh, worked with some ex-germans at least?}

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:28.240
Lily-senpai!

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:31.030
I have been informed of your circumstances.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:37.660
Inexperienced as I may be, I will act as your tutor for language arts.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.040
This is where we're going to study?

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:46.800
Yes. Being surrounded by nature has a 
relaxing effect, and it allows for easier learning.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.590
She's right, I feel great!

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.680
I feel like I can learn anything!

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:54.600
Me too!

00:06:54.600 --> 00:07:00.230
Judging by your report cards, Yume-san appears to struggle with kanji.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.190
Yeah, that's exactly right.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.860
I have problems with four-character idioms.

00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:12.990
Even after I memorize them through repetition, 
it all seems to slip away once I'm in front of a test.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:16.620
Kanji are vital to scoring well.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:22.420
I would normally recommend reading literature, but for now we must prioritize efficiency.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.750
Kanji are to be learned through the body!

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:38.350
With this, the kanji will be drilled in through the movement of your body, leaving their marks on your mind!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:39.230
Stop!

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:40.230
Upturn!

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.230
Taper!

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:43.730
Mindless absorption. {of course we could just write "mugamuchuu", but, yeah}{I wonder what would response if we just wrote 無我夢中}

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:48.820
It means to utterly lose oneself in pursuit of a goal.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.150
That's so cool! {thank god we don't do Pripara, who has a character who literally speaks in these}

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:54.120
It feels more like a performance than plain old kanji studying!

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.990
Now we can memorize them and have fun too!

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.000
With brush in hand, let us do it together.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.000
Okay!

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.630
Next up is math.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.710
We're meeting up here?

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:10.260
It's about time you showed up.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:13.470
Huh?!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.680
Ako is our math teacher?!

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:20.770
I am the tick tick ding-dong idol with a mental database, after all. {I love this formation of calling yourself a title, and I guess this way of writing is right}{I like this}

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.810
Who could possibly be a better math tutor for you?

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.480
Now that you mention it...

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:29.570
Ako-sensei, please give us the best math lesson you can!

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:36.570
These trigonometry problems are a cinch if you use real paper to solve them. {technically she says "picture problems"}{well, it's a little different from that}

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.530
With origami!

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.290
What do you think you're doing, Rola?!

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:48.380
Huh? Sorry, my hand folded on its own.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:54.550
I just don't get math. I just can't care to...

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.300
Oh really, is that so?

00:08:56.300 --> 00:09:00.810
And yet you still call yourself a proper idol, Sakuraba Rola?

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:06.190
You simply don't understand the inextricable relationship between idols and math.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.730
What do you mean?

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:09.440
I'll give an example.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:14.780
<i>x</i> pens costing 120 yen each are sold, leaving <i>y</i> remaining.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:16.990
What does that bring to mind?

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.490
That nobody cares.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:21.370
Okay, so what if I phrase it like this?

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:26.710
Rola sold <i>x</i> tickets to her concert, but still has <i>y</i> left over.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:32.250
Now, how would you set up the equation if you applied it to your show?

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:35.800
Um, if the venue has 500 seats...

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:38.220
See? Doesn't that motivate you to solve it?

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:44.180
The number of seats in the hall, how many tickets there are, your fan satisfaction rate, and more.

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:48.480
Math and calculations of all sorts surround idols!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.150
You're right!

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:52.230
Math is another kind of Aikatsu!

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:53.690
Exactly!

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:57.610
Anyone striving to be an idol must make math their ally.

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.570
I'm all fired up!

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:02.490
Let's solve the next problem together!

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:03.990
Okay!

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:06.750
Thank you, Senpai.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:10.210
It's no problem showing you the way.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:12.880
This school is so big that it's easy to get lost.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.130
That room...

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:20.220
That's the forbidden room from the rumors.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:27.980
A-A ghost?!{I would probably personally monster}{good point, but we see Kirara dressed(?) like a ghost later}

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.660
Be careful, I think I saw it!

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.870
So there really is a ghost!

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:45.370
In the forbidden room, right?

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.370
Oh no!

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:48.790
So scary...

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:51.130
Have you heard those strange rumors?

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:54.090
D-Dunno...

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.050
Kirara doesn't know!

00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:00.260
I've never even gotten close to that forbidden room.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:03.050
Perhaps I should report it to Elza.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.760
Ah, no! You can't!

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:08.520
Saying anything like that to Elza-sama is baa!

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:13.020
I-It's Caroline's snack time.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.360
Suspicious.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.320
Here's the last place.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:22.660
Wh—It's the S4 dorm!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.740
Then that means...

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.580
Yah-hoi!

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.040
Yuzu-senpai?!

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:35.250
Yuzu-senpai, we'll be relying on you for our English lesson!

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.550
Okay!

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.880
Why'd you ask Yuzu-senpai?

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:45.010
It seems she has no problem speaking English even though she's never studied it.

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.760
What? Seriously?

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:50.230
Come to think of it, Onee-chan said something similar.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:54.020
She's never actually seen Yuzu-senpai study before.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.560
That's amazing!

00:11:55.560 --> 00:12:02.320
Yeah, I feel like she's the perfect teacher for someone who's bad at English like me. {no, she is literally the worst. people who are naturals have no idea how to teach}{yeah, but that's not how she feels}

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:04.870
Mahiru-chan, you're not good at English?

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.450
No, not really.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.700
But French is right up your alley.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:09.950
I'm back.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:12.080
Ta-da!

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:16.790
I brought a taped foreign musical masterpiece. I figured we could watch it together. {do kids these days even know what "taped" means? it's like the floppy disk save symbol}

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:20.170
And I bought these from Ko-cafe for our snack. {it doesn't have the special e in the title}{I think this was before as well}

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:23.130
Eastern parfaits! They look delicious!

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:26.050
Let's all take it easy together!

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.950
That was so interesting! {and in fact, all the way back from episode 2}

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.910
My tummy is full.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.950
Still, will this really help us learn English?

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:56.920
Watching a musical in English gets us used to hearing it spoken and makes it less intimating.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:59.090
That was the idea, wasn't it?

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:01.420
I see. That's deep!

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.670
Yuzu just wanted to watch it!

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:04.470
Huh?

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.890
Thanks for hanging out with me!

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:10.720
I'm tired, but I had a good time.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.810
It was interesting experiencing different ways of studying.{longhood}

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.980
We're a little more prepared for the test now.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:21.230
For everyone who took the time to tutor us, 
let's make sure to get good grades!

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.070
Yeah!

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.570
Studying is Aikatsu too!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:27.740
Aikatsu! Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:13:57.310 --> 00:14:00.060
How did you do on language arts and math?

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.690
Great! I think I nailed it.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:05.570
It's all thanks to our tutors.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.450
All that's left is English.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.780
Everyone, may I have your attention?

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:14.660
The third exam period was to be for English, but Elza has come up with another idea.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:17.870
We'll be giving you a different kind of test this time.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:18.670
Huh?

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:27.880
You see, film crews and interviewers have come from far away to cover Elza's performance.{I don't think she's the kind of person to use likely as an adverb}{ehh, I guess we use overseas enough later}

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:31.640
Welcome to Venus Ark. I'm glad to see you.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:34.560
They've expressed interest in filming the students of Venus Ark as well.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:37.640
It's a chance for you to get some exposure.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:44.230
In place of the proficiency test, you'll be conducting interviews with Americans entirely in English.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.360
Do you like Elza?

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.490
Yes! Because...

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.620
Next up is you three. This way.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:58.750
Yes!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.500
Please tell me some Japanese culture.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:09.300
She wants us to share part of our culture from Japan.

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.050
I'm not prepared for this...

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:13.430
What should we tell her?

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:18.520
Yes! I got a good idea!

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.150
This is <i>shodou</i>. {I'm serious}

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:27.900
And karate!

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.580
This is origami!{they are using so many japanese words in their english test}

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.880
This is Japanese sweets!

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:51.050
And <i>sukonbu</i>!

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.840
Wow! Wonderful!

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.760
I have a azuki.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:57.430
I have a parfait! {I sincerely hope you know this meme}{I have a meme}

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:58.350
Those girls are doing pretty well.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:03.850
When this airs overseas, there's sure to be a positive reaction.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:06.060
Splendid.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:09.190
Thank goodness it went all right.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:11.740
That was inspired, Yume-chan.

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:12.700
Thanks.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:17.240
I took hints from everything we studied before.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:23.540
I guess it goes to show you never know when the things you learn will come in handy. {hello moral in point}

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.500
That's right.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:33.630
After this they're going to record Elza-sama's performance.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:38.180
Isn't Music Time a super famous music show in America?

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:42.390
I heard they sent in tons of requests for her to make an appearance.

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:47.860
That's amazing! I wonder how it feels to have fans across the world...

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:56.700
Just thinking about it makes it hard to contain my excitement!

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:04.210
Star Wings are the mark of a Star Premium Rare Coord.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:07.460
Dresses strengthen me.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:31.480
For I am perfect!

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:27.200
Music Time was great!

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:30.830
Our interviews made it in too!

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:33.290
It looks like we have more foreign fans now.

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:37.000
I've been getting flooded with messages on kirakiLINE since it aired. {um, I think I forgot to capitalize it properly before}{I think you did}

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:41.800
The results of our proficiency tests have been posted.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.430
Yay, I passed!

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:47.600
Me too!

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.350
I made it!

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:52.180
Congrats! I passed too.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:55.230
I'm telling you, there's really a ghost!

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:57.360
Got it. I'll check it out.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:13.250
The forbidden room...

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:17.380
S-See? I can hear a weird sound...

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.770
You found me.

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:40.360
Kirara-chan?!

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:43.030
Kirara was just playing a game.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:46.910
Japanese games are so fun! I got hooked!

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:49.030
It's the best!

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:51.790
But why would you play here?

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:57.540
I figured Elza-sama would be mad if she found out I was gaming before the tests, so I hid here.

00:21:57.540 --> 00:22:00.670
Oh, but I made sure to study too.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:03.920
Then that rumor about the ghost...

00:22:03.920 --> 00:22:08.300
I spread it around so nobody would come!

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:10.760
What, that's it?

00:22:10.760 --> 00:22:12.140
You're so silly.

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:13.350
Good grief.

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:15.560
But that's just like you!

00:22:16.810 --> 00:22:19.600
But! Scaring everyone like that is...

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:20.940
Baa!

00:22:21.730 --> 00:22:23.440
I'm sorry!

00:23:56.080 --> 00:24:00.040
The Blooming Queen Coord entrances fans from around the world.

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:01.750
I can't contain my excitement!

00:24:01.750 --> 00:24:05.290
Elza's perfect performance is truly beautiful.

00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:09.340
Star Wings that can charm the world are really intriguing.

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:13.050
The kind of sky that's above us today is...

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:14.640
One-hundred percent chance of Aikatsu!

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:17.810
Wait, who's that?

00:24:17.810 --> 00:24:19.640
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:19.640 --> 00:24:21.890
Expand the circle of Aikatsu!

00:24:21.890 --> 00:24:24.190
Become the first-star idol!
